And then you have to integrate it.

939
00:37:55.160 --> 00:37:56.280
Like, yes, we're—

940
00:37:56.280 --> 00:37:58.060
We also are clowns.

941
00:37:59.180 --> 00:38:00.540
Nursing gets so hard.

942
00:38:00.540 --> 00:38:01.660
We need something fun.

943
00:38:01.760 --> 00:38:04.900
After our shift, we do a full clown show.

944
00:38:05.040 --> 00:38:06.460
There was no teacher to go.

945
00:38:06.640 --> 00:38:07.080
Yeah.

946
00:38:07.200 --> 00:38:07.800
No teacher to say.

947
00:38:07.800 --> 00:38:09.980
We would get notes afterwards from our coach.

948
00:38:10.100 --> 00:38:12.760
And they'd be like, once again, they were nurses.

949
00:38:12.800 --> 00:38:15.080
And you decided to make them clowns.

950
00:38:15.160 --> 00:38:15.920
Yeah, I thought it was funny.

951
00:38:16.120 --> 00:38:17.120
We came in with the clowns.

952
00:38:17.400 --> 00:38:19.020
That scene wasn't going anywhere.

953
00:38:19.380 --> 00:38:20.800
Anyway, so—

954
00:38:20.800 --> 00:38:22.560
I really kicked it up a notch.

955
00:38:23.260 --> 00:38:27.180
Anyway, but sometimes you do have people like that in improv.

956
00:38:27.180 --> 00:38:28.480
And that was Michael Scott.

957
00:38:28.740 --> 00:38:29.740
He was the steamroller.

958
00:38:30.460 --> 00:38:32.120
Yeah, you totally have people like that.

959
00:38:32.280 --> 00:38:35.880
But I thought you brought some of your own life experience to Chris, the improv teacher.

960
00:38:36.060 --> 00:38:38.680
Because your background is improv and sketch comedy.

961
00:38:39.160 --> 00:38:43.080
And were there—it must have been sort of a very organic fit for you.

962
00:38:43.180 --> 00:38:45.560
Yeah, I didn't teach that much.

963
00:38:45.700 --> 00:38:47.660
But being in class, there's always that guy.

964
